    "https://macalester.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/US-Saint-Paul-MN/Senior-Network-Administrator_R2026260": {
      "title": "Senior Network Administrator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nOverview Plans, configures, installs, and maintains the college’s data network communications. Manages WAN, LAN, security, and wireless systems as well as mentor junior networking staff. Participates in efforts to develop strategies for on-premise and cloud systems connectivity, as well as manage disaster recovery and business continuity planning. Troubleshoots, installs, and configures networking components, as well as manage projects. Responsibilities & Qualifications Campus and Data Center Networking Manages data center networking, including core routing, core switching, load balancers, and fiber optic connectivity. Administers campus networking, including wireless controllers, wireless access points, and access switches. Participates in the Infrastructure on-call notification system. Network Applications, Security, and Services Administers network applications including IPAM, DHCP, DNS, VoIP and IPTV. Manages network monitoring and reporting tools to measure performance and service availability. Supports network security systems for authentication, encryption and firewall policies. Internet and Cloud Computing Supports cloud computing technologies, including implementation and migration of on-premise services to cloud/hosted environments.  Assists in developing and maintaining an ongoing plan for integrating cloud services to meet campus needs. Supervises campus internet connections, including managing ISP relationships, WAN connectivity, and site-to-site connections. Backup and Disaster Recovery Assists in disaster recovery planning and connectivity, this includes connectivity to remote and cloud datacenters. Maintains regular network configuration and server backups. Provides backup support in the absence of other team members. 3rd party Coordination Works with outside vendors and contractors on network related projects. Other Responsibilities: Completes other responsibilities as assigned. Participates as an active member of the team. Participates in department and college activities and supports implementation of shared goals and initiatives. Provides backup support to other members of the team. Required Qualifications: Bachelors Degree in Computer Science, Networking or equivalent degree required and/or combination of experience and relevant industry certifications (CCNP, JNCIS, etc) Minimum 5 years' experience with data networks, network-related systems administration, or other relevant IT experience required Experience with protocols such as BGP and OSPF and equipment from Juniper, Aruba and Palo Alto Networks strongly preferred Compensation : $97,392.00-$101,819.00 Annually Union: MAPE Benefits At Macalester, we are proud to offer excellent comprehensive employee benefits. Here are some highlights: 10% employer contributions to the retirement plan. Outstanding vacation and sick time packages, plus an additional 10 holidays. Competitive health, dental, vision, and life & disability insurance Generous employer contribution to Health Savings Account. Tuition assistance which pays between 75% - 90% of eligible tuition for employee dependents at select institutions. Free primary care for most services through Nice Healthcare when enrolled in a Macalester health plan. Access to the athletics fitness facility, wellness coaching, and activities. These are just some of the great benefits Macalester has to offer! To see our full benefits packages and options, please visit our Benefits Page Bargaining units may have slightly different benefits negotiated in their contracts. Please see applicable contracts for more details.   Satisfactory completion of a criminal background check is a condition of employment. Application Guidelines For best consideration, please submit your cover letter and resume through the Macalester Employment Opportunities webpage as soon as possible.   Macalester College does not discriminate on the grounds of sex, gender identity, race, color, national origin, age, religion, creed, disability, marital status, familial status, pregnancy, genetic information, membership or activity in a local human rights commission, veteran status, sexual orientation, status with regard to public assistance, or other categories protected by law. For additional information, see Macalester College's full Notice of Nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://macalester.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/US-Saint-Paul-MN/Admissions-Application-Reader-1_R2026287": {
      "title": "Admissions Application Reader-1",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nOverview The Macalester College Admissions Office seeks multiple Seasonal Remote Application Readers to support our full-time staff in the application review process for our upcoming application rounds. This position supports full-time staff in reviewing and evaluating admissions applications by assessing candidate materials while synthesizing and writing succinct and informative comments to be shared with the Admissions Committee. Candidates are encouraged to carefully review the description below and include a preference of schedule and availability clearly in their application materials. This position is entirely remote. There are no in-person working hours or assignments. Candidates are expected to work from within the United States and be able to provide their own computer with reliable internet access and audio/video capabilities. The position is not eligible for employment visa sponsorship. At Macalester, we are guided by our core values of academic excellence, internationalism, multiculturalism, and civic engagement. We believe in the transformative power of a liberal arts education that prepares students to flourish in a complex, interconnected world and to make a positive difference in their communities. Responsibilities & Qualifications Through the committee-based evaluation model, Seasonal Remote Application Readers will work synchronously with full-time Admissions staff via Zoom to: Evaluate applications for admission according to the standards set by the Admissions Office Analyze applicants' high school curriculum, academic performance record, extracurricular involvements, and potential to contribute to the Macalester community Synthesize, write and edit a short narrative summary of the candidate’s application Ensure timely completion of application reviews within established timelines Scheduling Requirements: Candidates are expected to work 14-28 hours per week from November 2 – December 4 and January 4-30, as well as training and onboarding the week of October 22-30. Application readers work full-day shifts between 9:00am CST – 5:00pm CST up to four days per week. All candidates hired for this position will be offered five weeks of work in 2026 and four weeks of work in 2027. Application volume and demand for admissions application readers is subject to change and influence available hours beyond the above guarantee.   We are requiring a cover letter with your resume submission when you apply. Strong preference will be given to candidates with work availability between 9:00am CST – 5:00pm CST on Mondays, Tuesdays, Thursdays and Fridays.  Qualifications:  It is expected that an employee in this role:  Bachelor’s degree. Have an appreciation for the value of a liberal arts education. Possess knowledge of the overall landscape of selective higher education. Exercise a high level of discretion and sensitive judgement and must be able to utilize a background of professional knowledge and experience to interpret guidelines which will apply to a large, complex, detailed array of objective and subjective information. All information is highly sensitive and confidential. Demonstrate a high proficiency with technology and web-based applications as all applicant files are reviewed electronically via an online platform. Have access to a home workspace, including a personal computer with up-to-date security and internet browser, access to reliable internet and audio/video capabilities. Demonstrate a commitment to Macalester’s mission and values. Preferred qualifications include: Direct experience as a student or staff member at a highly selective liberal arts college. Direct experience working in college access, college admissions, and/or college counseling. Possess knowledge of and/or sensitivity to issues related to the multiple backgrounds and experiences students come with and may write about in their application. Candidates may not be: Concurrently employed by or enrolled as a student at Macalester. Concurrently reading applications for another college or university. Currently employed as a high school/CBO counselor or independent admissions counselor/consultant Compensation : $20.60-$21.43 Hourly Benefits At Macalester, we are proud to offer excellent comprehensive employee benefits. Here are some highlights: 10% employer contributions to the retirement plan Outstanding vacation and sick time packages, plus an additional 10 holidays Competitive health, dental, vision, and life & disability insurance Generous employer contribution to Health Savings Account Tuition assistance which pays between 75% - 90% of eligible tuition for employee dependents at select institutions Free primary care for most services through Nice Healthcare when enrolled in a Macalester health plan Access to the athletics fitness facility, wellness coaching, and activities These are just some of the great benefits Macalester has to offer! To see our full benefits packages and options, please visit our Benefits Page   Satisfactory completion of a criminal background check is a condition of employment. Application Guidelines For best consideration, please submit your cover letter and resume through the Macalester Employment Opportunities webpage by September 11th. No applications will be received after this date.   Jaclyn Howard  Talent Acquisition Manager jhoward3@macalester.edu Macalester College does not discriminate on the grounds of sex, gender identity, race, color, national origin, age, religion, creed, disability, marital status, familial status, pregnancy, genetic information, membership or activity in a local human rights commission, veteran status, sexual orientation, status with regard to public assistance, or other categories protected by law. For additional information, see Macalester College's full Notice of Nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://macalester.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/US-Saint-Paul-MN/Mental-Health-Counselor_R2026367": {
      "title": "Mental Health Counselor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOverview As part of the integrated Hamre Center team, the mental health counselor provides short-term, individual, and group mental health counseling and prepares appropriate and timely documentation and reports. Collaborates closely with counseling and medical colleagues as appropriate. Participates in the Division of Student Affairs and other campus committees as assigned. Provides collaborative community education programming, trainings and/or outreach services. The Hamre Center for Health & Wellness is an integrated center with medical, counseling, operations/administrative, and health promotion/sexual respect teams who value a public health approach. Our team of directors is highly collaborative and operates in a distributed leadership model, in conjunction with our executive director. We care deeply about meeting our students where they are developmentally and partnering with them in decision-making about their care. Inclusion, access, and culturally responsive care are hallmarks of our Center; as such, we do not bill students for clinician time. We also value supporting the personal sustainability of our staff. We are active in developing the next generation of learners working in college health and regularly host counseling interns, an adolescent health fellow, medical residents, and medical assistant students. Additionally, Princeton Review recently ranked Macalester as #1 in Best Student Support and Counseling Services. Responsibilities & Qualifications Counseling Department The Counseling Department is a group of six individuals with intersecting identities and various therapeutic educational backgrounds who have a commitment to equitable health and healing for our student population while balancing a sustainable and collaborative work environment with each other. We use an integrated health approach with our Medical, Operations, and Health Promotion teams while uplifting continued education around clinical practice and community engagement with campus partners and community stakeholders. This team is proud of our 95%+ student satisfaction every semester for the past three years.  Responsibilities:  60% Provides short-term, individual, and group mental health counseling. Provides referral guidance and consultation services to students, parents/families (with ROI), and the larger campus community as appropriate.  This includes crisis response coverage such as Same Day appointments and contribution to campus-wide incident response at the discretion of the Director of Counseling and the Executive Director. 20% Prepares appropriate and timely documentation and reports.  10% Participates in the Division of Student Affairs and other campus committees as assigned. Provides collaborative community education programming, trainings, outreach and engagement services.  5% Ongoing professional development.  5% Completes other responsibilities as assigned. Participates as an active member of the team. Participates in department and college activities and supports implementation of shared goals and initiatives. Provides backup support to other members of the team.     Qualifications:    Master’s degree required.  Must be fully licensed (or license-eligible) in the state of Minnesota for practice in stated counseling-related field (e.g. LICSW, LMFT, LPCC, LP, ATR) .  Preferred qualifications Experience working in a college counseling center, comprehensive knowledge of culturally responsive evidence-based and theory-driven mental health practices, including but not limited to, short term therapy models, assessment, crisis intervention, individual and group counseling, trauma-informed care; experience with a wide range of intersecting identities, understanding of historical and intergenerational trauma, and emphasis on the impact of systemic oppression on macro to micro scales.  This position is 39 weeks full-time from mid-August to mid-May.  Upon successful onboarding, counseling staff is eligible for up to 20% remote work. Compensation : $52,994.00-$56,489.00 Annually Benefits At Macalester, we are proud to offer excellent comprehensive employee benefits. Here are some highlights: 10% employer contributions to the retirement plan Outstanding vacation and sick time packages, plus an additional 10 holidays Competitive health, dental, vision, and life & disability insurance Generous employer contribution to Health Savings Account Tuition assistance which pays between 75% - 90% of eligible tuition for employee dependents at select institutions Free primary care for most services through Nice Healthcare when enrolled in a Macalester health plan Access to the athletics fitness facility, wellness coaching, and activities These are just some of the great benefits Macalester has to offer! To see our full benefits packages and options, please visit our Benefits Page   Satisfactory completion of a criminal background check is a condition of employment. Application Guidelines For best consideration, please submit your cover letter and resume through the Macalester Employment Opportunities webpage by September 14th. No applications will be received after this date.   Jaclyn Howard  Talent Acquisition Manager jhoward3@macalester.edu Macalester College does not discriminate on the grounds of sex, gender identity, race, color, national origin, age, religion, creed, disability, marital status, familial status, pregnancy, genetic information, membership or activity in a local human rights commission, veteran status, sexual orientation, status with regard to public assistance, or other categories protected by law. For additional information, see Macalester College's full Notice of Nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://macalester.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/US-Saint-Paul-MN/Student-Employment-Learning---Development-Manager_R2026350": {
      "title": "Student Employment Learning & Development Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOverview Leads the strategic development of student employment as a high-impact educational practice. Reimagines student employment as a meaningful learning experience that integrates professional skill development, mentorship, and career readiness competencies into on-campus work. Works closely with the Student Employment Program Manager and collaborates with key stakeholders such as Financial Aid, Human Resources, and the Career Exploration team to design, assess, and sustain a student employment program that aligns with institutional learning goals and enhances student success. About the Department: Career Exploration seeks to empower and guide students and alumni by providing comprehensive career advising and opportunities to connect within and beyond the Macalester community. We are dedicated to ensuring equitable access to resources and experiential learning for skill-building and self-discovery. We believe in continuous learning and support a self-driven approach towards finding purpose and fulfillment. This is a hybrid position, 3 days a week in the office with the option to work 2 days a week from home. The daily work hours are 8:00 am-4:30 pm Monday through Friday. Responsibilities & Qualifications Responsibilities:  Program Management and Strategy: Leads the transformation of student employment into a high-impact educational practice including learning outcomes aligned with the institutional mission. Establishes program goals and creates tools to assess student learning and program effectiveness, working closely with campus partners to foster a culture of feedback, reflection, and professional development, while also providing training to supervisors to strengthen the evaluation process. Reviews and revises existing job descriptions to incorporate learning goals and skill development opportunities, and collaborate with supervisors to incorporate NACE career competencies into job descriptions. Partners with the Student Employment Program Manager, academic departments, Career Exploration, Student Affairs, Financial Aid, and Human Resources to align student employment with institutional strategic plans and initiatives. Ensures compliance with federal and state laws and institutional student employment regulations and policies. Collaborates on cross-functional initiatives and projects related to student employment, workforce planning, operational efficiency, and administrative processes. Ensures equitable access to on-campus employment opportunities and champion inclusive supervision practices across all campus departments. Student and Staff Professional Development and Programming: Designs and delivers training for student employees focused on professional skills and helps students develop and translate key skills from their student employment experiences to life beyond Macalester. Develops and facilitates training for staff and faculty supervisors on providing effective mentorship, supervision, and skill development. Establishes a network or roundtable series for faculty and staff supervisors to share best practices in mentorship and student management. Creates resources for supervisors (workshops, toolkits, etc.) for ongoing learning and training . Communication and Data: Maintains student employment web content, documentation, communications, and related educational materials for students and departments. Analyzes student employment data to identify trends, risks, and opportunities for process improvement, and prepare reports/recommendations for operational enhancements to improve consistency, compliance, and efficiency. Maintains accurate records and documentation related to student employment. Performs other duties as assigned including: Participates as an active member of the team Participates in department and college activities and supports implementation of shared goals and initiatives Provides backup support to other members of the team Qualifications:  Bachelor’s degree and 3–5 years of relevant experience, or a master’s degree and 1–3 years of relevant experience. Experience in student employment, experiential learning, career development, workforce development, or a related field. Demonstrated ability to design and deliver training or educational programs.  Strong project management, communication, and organizational skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively, manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines.  Proficiency with technology and software used to manage programs, systems, and processes, including Handshake and Google Workspace. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree Experience designing, launching, and sustaining a new program, particularly in a higher education setting. Experience evaluating programs using qualitative and quantitative data to inform improvements and decision-making Compensation : $62,135.00-$64,959.00 Annually Union: MAPE Benefits At Macalester, we are proud to offer excellent comprehensive employee benefits. Here are some highlights: 10% employer contributions to the retirement plan. Outstanding vacation and sick time packages, plus an additional 10 holidays. Competitive health, dental, vision, and life & disability insurance Generous employer contribution to Health Savings Account. Tuition assistance which pays between 75% - 90% of eligible tuition for employee dependents at select institutions. Free primary care for most services through Nice Healthcare when enrolled in a Macalester health plan. Access to the athletics fitness facility, wellness coaching, and activities. These are just some of the great benefits Macalester has to offer! To see our full benefits packages and options, please visit our Benefits Page Bargaining units may have slightly different benefits negotiated in their contracts. Please see applicable contracts for more details.   Satisfactory completion of a criminal background check is a condition of employment. Application Guidelines For best consideration, please submit your cover letter and resume through the Macalester Employment Opportunities webpage by September 4th. No applications will be received after this date.   Jaclyn Howard   Talent Acquisition Manager jhoward3@macalester.edu   Macalester College does not discriminate on the grounds of sex, gender identity, race, color, national origin, age, religion, creed, disability, marital status, familial status, pregnancy, genetic information, membership or activity in a local human rights commission, veteran status, sexual orientation, status with regard to public assistance, or other categories protected by law. For additional information, see Macalester College's full Notice of Nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://macalester.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/US-Saint-Paul-MN/Operating-Engineer_R2026351": {
      "title": "Operating Engineer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOverview Macalester College seeks to hire an Operating Engineer to work in its Facilities Services Department during the academic year. This position will be responsible for monitoring, maintenance, and operation of the central heating plant high-pressure boiler system and central chillers during the academic year, September thru May. and is responsible for general campus maintenance duties during the summer. Hours/Schedule: 40 Hours - Third Shift Compensation: $45.68 per Hour This is a union position. After the 6 month probationary period, the successful candidate will be required to join the International Union of Operating Engineers, Local Number 70. As the Operating Engineer, you will be part of a team that makes up a 3 shift around-the-clock operation monitoring and maintaining our high-pressure boilers during the heating season which is mid-October to mid-May. During this period the position is a Third Shift shift position (11pm-7am) On a rotating day pattern, 7-on, 2-off, 7-on, 2-off, 6-on, 4-off. Boiler schedules are created well in advance of the heating season to allow for scheduling. During the cooling season mid-May through mid-October the shift transitions to a maintenance position with a flexible shift schedule, typically 1st shift. Responsibilities & Qualifications Responsibilities: Testing, monitoring, maintenance, repair, and operation of high-pressure boilers and related equipment. Monitor boiler water quality and administer chemical treatment as indicated through testing. Monitor building automation systems to ensure proper temperature control and alarm response to campus buildings and equipment. Follows accepted process for adjustments to boiler plant equipment. Project schedule awareness, knowledge of and adherence to accepted best practices Perform preventive/predictive maintenance as directed. May perform testing, troubleshooting, repair, and maintenance of equipment and systems related to heating, ventilating, air conditioning, refrigeration, mechanical, electrical, and plumbing issues in campus buildings. This position will be part of the maintenance on-call rotation list Provide Central Plant support for special events on campus, which may include weekends and/or holidays. Follow safe work practices and all environmental, health and safety policies and procedures Engaging in and promoting Macalester’s culture of diversity and inclusion, encompassing individuals of any heritage, identity, status or orientation. Required    Minnesota First Class B Boiler Operator's license Possesses exceptional knowledge of high-pressure steam boiler operation, principles, applications, techniques, procedures and dangers of such systems. Must possess knowledge and skills in electricity, HVAC, and plumbing in sufficient depth to perform testing, maintenance, and repair of systems. Significant work experience with building energy management computer systems     Preferred   Associate's degree, or vocational or technical school degree in an equipment/building maintenance discipline 5 years experience maintaining equipment and systems in a high pressure boiler plant.   At Macalester , we are proud to offer excellent comprehensive employee benefits. Here are some highlights: 10% employer contributions to the retirement plan. UNION PENSION CONTRIBUTIONS Outstanding vacation and sick time packages, plus an additional 10 holidays. Generous employer contribution to Health Savings Account. Competitive health, dental, vision, and life & disability insurance.  Free primary care for most services through Nice Healthcare when enrolled in a Macalester health plan. Access to the athletics fitness facility, wellness coaching, and activities. These are just some of the great benefits Macalester has to offer! To see our full benefits packages and options, please visit our Benefits Page .   Satisfactory completion of a criminal background check is a condition of employment.   Compensation : $45.68-$45.68 Hourly Union: Local 70 - Engineers Benefits At Macalester, we are proud to offer excellent comprehensive employee benefits. Here are some highlights: 10% employer contributions to the retirement plan. Outstanding vacation and sick time packages, plus an additional 10 holidays. Competitive health, dental, vision, and life & disability insurance Generous employer contribution to Health Savings Account. Tuition assistance which pays between 75% - 90% of eligible tuition for employee dependents at select institutions. Free primary care for most services through Nice Healthcare when enrolled in a Macalester health plan. Access to the athletics fitness facility, wellness coaching, and activities. These are just some of the great benefits Macalester has to offer! To see our full benefits packages and options, please visit our Benefits Page Bargaining units may have slightly different benefits negotiated in their contracts. Please see applicable contracts for more details.   Satisfactory completion of a criminal background check is a condition of employment. Application Guidelines For best consideration, please submit your cover letter and resume through the Macalester Employment Opportunities webpage by September 7th. No applications will be received after this date.   Jaclyn Howard  Talent Acquisition Manager jhoward3@macalester.edu   Macalester College does not discriminate on the grounds of sex, gender identity, race, color, national origin, age, religion, creed, disability, marital status, familial status, pregnancy, genetic information, membership or activity in a local human rights commission, veteran status, sexual orientation, status with regard to public assistance, or other categories protected by law. For additional information, see Macalester College's full Notice of Nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://macalester.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/US-Saint-Paul-MN/Internal-Communications-Specialist_R2026352": {
      "title": "Internal Communications Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOverview Executes strategic communication plans that inform, engage, and connect the campus community. Serves as a bridge between the Communications and Marketing department and various campus partners. Ensures that institutional priorities, campus stories, and visual content are seamlessly aligned to foster a well-informed community. Responsibilities & Qualifications Coordinates, plans, and distributes content across primary internal communication channels (e.g., Mac Daily, internal announcements, and digital signage) in collaboration with the Communications & Marketing team. Acts as a strategic advisor to campus partners on best practices for reaching internal audiences effectively. Manages and maintains the college events calendar, collaborating with departments across campus to ensure timely, accurate, and engaging promotion of upcoming activities to the internal community. Assists with the production of the daily campus internal newsletter, the Mac Daily. Participates actively in team brainstorming sessions to align internal messaging with broader marketing and external relations efforts. Serves as the primary point of contact for campus partners requesting photography and visual content support related to campus events and student life. Manages the intake, vetting, and scheduling process for campus photo shoots, ensuring alignment with overarching communication goals and strategic priorities. Manages permissions (including talent and location releases) prior to handing shoots off to the creative team if required. Assists with loading files into Macalester’s digital asset management system when needed. Supports the AVP of Communications and Marketing with administrative duties. Supports with projects assigned by the AVP of Communications and Marketing. Serves on committees (as assigned) as department liaison. Monitors departmental email inbox. Other duties as assigned Other Responsibilities: Completes other responsibilities as assigned. Participates as an active member of the team. Participates in department and college activities and supports implementation of shared goals and initiatives. Provides backup support to other members of the team. Required Qualifications: Minimum of 3 years of experience in communications, public relations, internal relations, or a closely related field. Experience collaborating with creative teams (designers, videographers, photographers) to guide visual content creation. Exceptional writing, editing, and storytelling skills, with the ability to tailor messaging to diverse audiences. Strong project management and organizational skills with a demonstrated ability to coordinate schedules and logistics across multiple stakeholders. Proven experience managing internal communication channels or newsletters within a complex organization (higher education environment preferred). Compensation : $56,486.00-$59,054.00 Annually Union: MAPE Benefits At Macalester, we are proud to offer excellent comprehensive employee benefits. Here are some highlights: 10% employer contributions to the retirement plan. Outstanding vacation and sick time packages, plus an additional 10 holidays. Competitive health, dental, vision, and life & disability insurance Generous employer contribution to Health Savings Account. Tuition assistance which pays between 75% - 90% of eligible tuition for employee dependents at select institutions. Free primary care for most services through Nice Healthcare when enrolled in a Macalester health plan. Access to the athletics fitness facility, wellness coaching, and activities. These are just some of the great benefits Macalester has to offer! To see our full benefits packages and options, please visit our Benefits Page Bargaining units may have slightly different benefits negotiated in their contracts. Please see applicable contracts for more details.   Satisfactory completion of a criminal background check is a condition of employment. Application Guidelines For best consideration, please submit your required cover letter and resume through the Macalester Employment Opportunities webpage by September 7th. No applications will be received after this date. Careers website: https://www.macalester.edu/human-resources/jobs/   Jaclyn Howard  Talent Acquisition Manager jhoward3@macalester.edu Macalester College does not discriminate on the grounds of sex, gender identity, race, color, national origin, age, religion, creed, disability, marital status, familial status, pregnancy, genetic information, membership or activity in a local human rights commission, veteran status, sexual orientation, status with regard to public assistance, or other categories protected by law. For additional information, see Macalester College's full Notice of Nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://macalester.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/US-Saint-Paul-MN/Associate-Director-of-Alumni-Engagement_R2026281": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Alumni Engagement",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOverview Macalester College seeks an operationally sharp, systems-minded professional to serve as Assistant Director of Alumni Engagement, leading the college's annual Reunion program and supporting Alumni Board operations. This role is built for someone who can see the full picture, build the plan, close the gaps, and execute without waiting to be told what comes next. The ideal candidate brings proven experience in project management, volunteer coordination, and stakeholder communication, and is ready to own their work from strategy through implementation. This is a full-time, hybrid-eligible position with the option of Tuesday through Thursday in office and Monday and Friday remote. About the Engagement Team: Macalester's Engagement team works to expand and enrich the ways alumni and friends of the college connect with one another and with Macalester. Through events, volunteering, and giving opportunities, we cultivate lifelong relationships rooted in pride and purpose. We are committed to creativity, collaboration, and community-focused strategy, approach our work through an equity lens, and take pride in being innovative, inclusive, and impact-driven. Responsibilities & Qualifications Reunion Project Management & Communications Lead the operational planning and execution of Macalester's annual Reunion program, serving as the central point of coordination for logistics, communications, volunteer activities, and event execution. Develop and manage project plans, timelines, workback schedules, and implementation processes across Advancement, Special Events, Communications, and campus partners. Track project milestones, identify potential obstacles, and proactively communicate next steps and deadlines to all stakeholders. Manage committee requests, meeting schedules, documentation, and information flow to keep all parties organized and aligned. Design and document workflows that make Reunion processes repeatable and scalable year over year. Support efforts to leverage Reunion participation as a springboard for ongoing alumni engagement with the college. Develop, track, and evaluate key performance metrics, survey results, and participant feedback to assess program effectiveness and identify opportunities for continuous improvement. Monitor Reunion expenses and track budget activity throughout the year, providing regular updates and recommendations to help ensure programs and events remain within budget parameters.     Volunteer Management & Stewardship Develop and direct Reunion volunteer strategy in close collaboration with Advancement partners, including identifying and engaging key stakeholders and outreach to new volunteers. Coordinate recruitment, onboarding, training, and communications for Reunion volunteers, providing clear and consistent expectations, resources, and support. Serve as primary staff liaison for 1–3 Reunion Committees. Partner with Macalester Fund staff to coordinate Reunion class gift volunteer training and activities. Recruit, coordinate, and mentor campus volunteers and Reunion Student Coordinators. Assist with the recruitment, training, supervision, and support of Reunion student staff and Reunion Coordinators to ensure successful program execution and a positive volunteer experience.   Alumni Board Support Provide operational support for Alumni Board activities, enabling the Director of Alumni Engagement to focus on strategy and relationship-building. Coordinate meeting logistics, agendas, materials, timelines, and follow-up communications. Prepare and brief speakers; track action items and deliverables across board initiatives. Anticipate upcoming needs and ensure board projects remain organized and on schedule. Advise and engage Alumni Board Student Directors and oversee their annual project ensuring they have at least one group project each year. Serve as staff liaison for an Alumni Board committee, coordinating meetings, communications, project timelines, and follow-up actions to support the committee's goals and initiatives.  Alumni Engagement & Advancement Projects Contribute to additional programming, events, and initiatives throughout the year in collaboration with Advancement and campus partners, applying the same operational rigor and collaborative approach as formally assigned work. Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Engage in and promote Macalester's culture of diversity and inclusion, encompassing individuals of any heritage, identity, status, or orientation . Required Qualifications Demonstrated experience in project management, including building and managing timelines, workback schedules, and multi-stakeholder workflows. Experience in event management, volunteer coordination, or program administration in a complex organizational environment. Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to communicate clearly and persuasively across a variety of audiences and styles. Proven ability to prioritize and manage multiple competing projects in a fast-paced environment. Experience creating and maintaining organizational systems, process documentation, and operational workflows. Ability to anticipate gaps, solve problems proactively, and exercise sound judgment with limited supervision. Commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion, and experience working with individuals from a variety of backgrounds, identities, and perspectives.   Preferred Qualifications 5 or more years of progressively responsible experience leading programs or functions with significant independence (strongly preferred for Associate Director consideration). Experience designing and improving operational systems, not just executing within them. Demonstrated ability to manage across stakeholder groups, including volunteers, colleagues, and senior leaders. Experience supervising, mentoring, or managing junior staff or student employees. Familiarity with alumni engagement, advancement, or nonprofit relationship management. Experience in higher education Compensation : $62,135.00-$64,959.00 Union: MAPE Benefits At Macalester, we are proud to offer excellent comprehensive employee benefits. Here are some highlights: 10% employer contributions to the retirement plan. Outstanding vacation and sick time packages, plus an additional 10 holidays. Competitive health, dental, vision, and life & disability insurance Generous employer contribution to Health Savings Account. Tuition assistance which pays between 75% - 90% of eligible tuition for employee dependents at select institutions. Free primary care for most services through Nice Healthcare when enrolled in a Macalester health plan. Access to the athletics fitness facility, wellness coaching, and activities. These are just some of the great benefits Macalester has to offer! To see our full benefits packages and options, please visit our Benefits Page Bargaining units may have slightly different benefits negotiated in their contracts. Please see applicable contracts for more details.   Satisfactory completion of a criminal background check is a condition of employment. Application Guidelines For best consideration, please submit your cover letter and resume through the Macalester Employment Opportunities webpage by August 26th, 2026. No applications will be received after this date.   Kim Price Interim - Talent Acquisition Manager price@macalester.edu   Macalester College does not discriminate on the grounds of sex, gender identity, race, color, national origin, age, religion, creed, disability, marital status, familial status, pregnancy, genetic information, membership or activity in a local human rights commission, veteran status, sexual orientation, status with regard to public assistance, or other categories protected by law. For additional information, see Macalester College's full Notice of Nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://macalester.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/US-Saint-Paul-MN/Executive-Assistant_R2026293": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOverview The Executive Assistant to the VP of Administration and Finance and the VP for Institutional Equity is primarily responsible for providing a range of administrative services to the VPs in order to promote smooth functioning of the VP’s areas of responsibility. The primary tasks include administrative support, project and event management, reception, organizational functions, document management and distribution, incoming and outgoing communication with campus and external constituents, data gathering and presentation, managing schedules, invoicing, departmental budget tracking, and providing general support for others in their areas. Success is measured by the timeliness, accuracy, and completeness of the work and the professional nature of the delivery. This is a 12-month, full-time, hourly position, with expectations for in-office work. Some flexibility in scheduling for evenings and weekends may be required. Some remote-hybrid work may be possible during the summer. Responsibilities & Qualifications Institutional Equity leads Macalester’s ongoing commitment to equity and social justice through collective action, shared visioning, and community connection. The division includes the Center for Religious and Spiritual Life, equity education programs, the Lealtad-Suzuki Center for Social Justice, and the Title IX and Nondiscrimination Office. Institutional Equity works collaboratively across campus to facilitate programs, resources, and initiatives to promote a campus climate that is inclusive, affirming, and respectful. We support the advancement of equity in academic programs, student resources, recruitment and retention efforts, learning and work environments, professional development, resource stewardship, and overall institutional effectiveness. The Administration and Finance Division comprises five key areas of the college: Business Services, Human Resources, Facilities Services, High Winds (real estate management and neighborhood relations), and the college's endowment (long-term investments managed by an outsourced chief investment officer/firm (OCIO)). The Division staffs five Board of Trustees committees corresponding to these areas of oversight. Responsibilities:  Provide reception and administrative support: greet visitors and answer inquiries; maintain calendars, schedules meetings and makes travel arrangements; organize and maintain office records Prepare letters, memoranda, reports, presentations, websites, and other materials for meetings, events, and college communications Prepare on-line requisitioning of invoices; monitor budgets and track expenditures; purchase supplies and reconcile financial records Coordinate logistics for meetings, committees, and small events Act as liaison for the VPs with trustees, department heads, staff members and the public Provide support for preparation and presentation of materials for the Board of Trustees committees of the VP of Administration and Finance: Finance Committee, Audit & Risk Management Committee, and Infrastructure Committee; support Investment Committee as needed Provide support to Title IX and Nondiscrimination program, coordinate logistical details, communications, and website maintenance Provide support for the Institutional Equity division, coordinate logistical details and communications with campus and community partners, and website maintenance Provide back up support for the president’s & provost’s offices, as well as for the VPs’ respective staff; coordinate with staff in President’s suite and Academic Affairs suite Provide support for college-wide events and participate in the life of the college Qualifications:   Minimum education: High school diploma Preferred education: Associate’s degree, vocational or technical school degree, Bachelor’s degree, or equivalent Minimum three years of professional experience Knowledge of and commitment to equity and inclusion as imperative to a respectful learning and work environment Knowledge of and experience with financial reporting Experience in office management, calendar and meeting management, project and event management Advanced knowledge of Google Apps and Microsoft Office suite is required. Experience with document management software preferred but not required.  Excellent spreadsheet and reporting skills and ability to learn new software systems and applications. Demonstrated ability to interact respectfully and effectively in working with external constituents including trustees, students, colleagues, donors, alumni, campus visitors, cross-departmental colleagues, and vendors  Ability to create and execute administrative processes and project implementation along with effective prioritization of projects Highly effective interpersonal and written, communication and organizational skills Ability to anticipate needs, function independently, and exercise sound judgment Skilled in listening, anticipating, and responding to the needs of two Vice Presidents to achieve high quality customer service Compensation : $28.03-$29.31 Hourly Union: MAPE Benefits At Macalester, we are proud to offer excellent comprehensive employee benefits. Here are some highlights: 10% employer contributions to the retirement plan. Outstanding vacation and sick time packages, plus an additional 10 holidays. Competitive health, dental, vision, and life & disability insurance Generous employer contribution to Health Savings Account. Tuition assistance which pays between 75% - 90% of eligible tuition for employee dependents at select institutions. Free primary care for most services through Nice Healthcare when enrolled in a Macalester health plan. Access to the athletics fitness facility, wellness coaching, and activities. These are just some of the great benefits Macalester has to offer! To see our full benefits packages and options, please visit our Benefits Page Bargaining units may have slightly different benefits negotiated in their contracts. Please see applicable contracts for more details.   Satisfactory completion of a criminal background check is a condition of employment. Application Guidelines For best consideration, please submit your cover letter and resume through the Macalester Employment Opportunities webpage by August 31st, 2026. No applications will be received after this date.   Kim Price Interim - Talent Acquisition Manager price@macalester.edu   Macalester College does not discriminate on the grounds of sex, gender identity, race, color, national origin, age, religion, creed, disability, marital status, familial status, pregnancy, genetic information, membership or activity in a local human rights commission, veteran status, sexual orientation, status with regard to public assistance, or other categories protected by law. For additional information, see Macalester College's full Notice of Nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://macalester.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/US-Saint-Paul-MN/Assistant-Swimming---Diving--Coach_R2026282": {
      "title": "Assistant Swimming & Diving  Coach",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nOverview Macalester College seeks an Assistant Swimming & Diving Coach to support the leadership and direction of all phases of a successful and competitive NCAA Division III swimming and diving program. This position assists with team practices, competitions, recruiting, event management, and student-athlete development, and also assists with coaching Macalester’s Masters swimming program. The successful candidate will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and team-oriented environment that supports the athletic, academic, and personal development of student-athletes. This is a 12-month position with approximately 3–15 hours per week depending on the season; evening and weekend hours are required. About the Department: Macalester College Athletics is committed to providing an excellent student-athlete experience within a highly selective liberal arts college. The swimming and diving program emphasizes competitive excellence, academic achievement, personal growth, inclusion, and the holistic wellbeing of its student-athletes. The Assistant Swimming & Diving Coach will work collaboratively with the Head Coach and coaching staff to support the continued success and development of the program Responsibilities & Qualifications Responsibilities: Assist with planning and conducting safe, effective team practices. Provide coaching and instruction during practices and competitions. Assist with the supervision and operation of Masters swimming workouts. Support home meet preparation, recruiting, and other program events as needed. Assist with recruiting activities as needed. Promote a positive, inclusive, and team-oriented environment and represent Macalester and its athletics program with professionalism, integrity, and sportsmanship. Develop positive working relationships with student-athletes, families, coaches, officials, colleagues, and members of the campus and broader community. Qualifications:  Valid driver’s license required. 1–3+ years of collegiate swimming experience is preferred. Knowledge of swimming training methods, practice planning, and competitive strategies. Strong teaching, leadership, organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse ethnic, cultural, and socioeconomic backgrounds. General proficiency with current office and computer technology. Ability to contribute positively to a collaborative, team-oriented athletics department. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree preferred Compensation : $7,800.00-$7,800.00 Annually Benefits At Macalester, we are proud to offer excellent comprehensive employee benefits. Here are some highlights: 10% employer contributions to the retirement plan Outstanding vacation and sick time packages, plus an additional 10 holidays Competitive health, dental, vision, and life & disability insurance Generous employer contribution to Health Savings Account Tuition assistance which pays between 75% - 90% of eligible tuition for employee dependents at select institutions Free primary care for most services through Nice Healthcare when enrolled in a Macalester health plan Access to the athletics fitness facility, wellness coaching, and activities These are just some of the great benefits Macalester has to offer! To see our full benefits packages and options, please visit our Benefits Page   Satisfactory completion of a criminal background check is a condition of employment. Application Guidelines For best consideration, please submit your cover letter and resume through the Macalester Employment Opportunities webpage by August 26th, 2026. No applications will be received after this date.   Kim Price Interim - Talent Acquisition Manager price@macalester.edu   Macalester College does not discriminate on the grounds of sex, gender identity, race, color, national origin, age, religion, creed, disability, marital status, familial status, pregnancy, genetic information, membership or activity in a local human rights commission, veteran status, sexual orientation, status with regard to public assistance, or other categories protected by law. For additional information, see Macalester College's full Notice of Nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://macalester.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/US-Saint-Paul-MN/Public-Safety-Officer_R2026273": {
      "title": "Public Safety Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOverview Patrols building interiors/exteriors and parking facilities. Monitors ongoing campus security issues. Responds to requests for assistance. Provides initial response as needed, including first aid. Directs scene activities and coordinates communication with internal and/or external agencies as needed. Performs other related duties as assigned. Responsibilities & Qualifications Protects life, safeguards property and maintains peace and order on the college campus through enforcement of local, state, and federal laws as well as college rules and regulations. Pro-actively patrols a residential community and prevents crime. Responds to emergency situations and works closely with local police and emergency services personnel. Conducts preliminary investigations involving criminal or suspicious activities. Prepares, writes and files reports. Other Responsibilities: Completes other responsibilities as assigned. Participates as an active member of the team. Participates in department and college activities and supports implementation of shared goals and initiatives. Provides backup support to other members of the team. Required Qualifications: High School Diploma Minimum 1 year of experience and knowledge of procedures for effective security, codes and regulations related to the work, law enforcement Understanding procedures, terminology, and techniques for dealing with a variety of individuals from various socioeconomic, ethnic and cultural backgrounds, in person, often where relations may be confrontational or strained. Compensation : $23.19-$24.25 Hourly Benefits At Macalester, we are proud to offer excellent comprehensive employee benefits. Here are some highlights: 10% employer contributions to the retirement plan Outstanding vacation and sick time packages, plus an additional 10 holidays Competitive health, dental, vision, and life & disability insurance Generous employer contribution to Health Savings Account Tuition assistance which pays between 75% - 90% of eligible tuition for employee dependents at select institutions Free primary care for most services through Nice Healthcare when enrolled in a Macalester health plan Access to the athletics fitness facility, wellness coaching, and activities These are just some of the great benefits Macalester has to offer! To see our full benefits packages and options, please visit our Benefits Page   Satisfactory completion of a criminal background check is a condition of employment. Application Guidelines For best consideration, please submit your cover letter and resume through the Macalester Employment Opportunities webpage by August 18th, 2026. No applications will be received after this date.   Kim Price Interim - Talent Acquisition Manager price@macalester.edu   Macalester College does not discriminate on the grounds of sex, gender identity, race, color, national origin, age, religion, creed, disability, marital status, familial status, pregnancy, genetic information, membership or activity in a local human rights commission, veteran status, sexual orientation, status with regard to public assistance, or other categories protected by law. For additional information, see Macalester College's full Notice of Nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://macalester.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/US-Saint-Paul-MN/Director-of-Engagement-Communication_R2026263": {
      "title": "Director of Engagement Communications",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOverview The Director of Engagement Communications creates, manages, and directs alumni and constituent communications that promote a lifelong relationship with the College. This position leads strategy, implementation, and analysis for engaging alumni and parents and families, cultivating and stewarding their relationships with the College with a goal of ultimately increasing philanthropic support . A central part of this work is crafting fundraising solicitations, stewardship messages, and impact reporting in close collaboration with the AVP of Engagement. The director will also set and facilitate regular strategy and content development meetings with colleagues across engagement and advancement, serving as a strategic partner across teams and creating a holistic communications experience for our constituents. Working within a shared production model, the director partners with content-providing offices across Advancement, allowing the director to focus on strategy, writing, and quality, while staying current on digital communications best practices and driving continuous innovation in the field. About the Department When students choose Macalester, they join a lifelong community of support. The Macalester Engagement department—made up of the alumni engagement, annual giving, parent and family, and special events teams—fosters meaningful relationships with students, alumni, and parents through increasing levels of engagement with the college over a lifetime. Our work is about growing the number of constituents who connect with Macalester: inspiring active engagement through campus- and volunteer-driven events, fostering community, connecting audiences to volunteer opportunities, and building philanthropic journeys. Responsibilities & Qualifications Lead Strategic Vision:   Design and execute a strategic communications plan that strengthens constituent engagement while balancing needs of the Engagement team and wider College Collaborate with the Macalester Fund and Alumni Engagement teams to achieve shared goals for alumni engagement, philanthropic education, solicitation, retention, and advancement Work closely with the Marketing and Communications team to create unified messaging for alumni outreach that aligns with College-wide communications, incorporating industry best practices and innovative communications techniques As a leader on the Engagement Team, participate in setting office-wide strategies to further the division’s equity-grounded principles and the college’s strategic priorities Communication Strategy, Solicitation Writing, and Execution Partner with the Macalester Fund director and Parent & Family Engagement director to develop strategy and write persuasive fundraising solicitations, stewardship communications, and impact reporting for multi-channel, multi-segmented campaigns, with a goal of increasing donor support for the College’s operating budget Collaborate with the Engagement Directors to design targeted approaches to engage distinct constituent segments including students, recent graduates, young alumni, mid-career alumni, identity & affinity groups, parents & families, and regionally based groups  Guide the Engagement team’s shared email production model: set standards, timelines, and quality controls for broadcast email, including strategic calendaring; create, maintain, and upgrade systems to communicate at scale on behalf of campus partners as appropriate; represent Engagement for large-scale event communication strategy; and build and send high-priority emails as needed using a responsive email framework (HTML/MJML) and the Slate Deliver platform Demonstrate interest in digital best practices and tools to support effective email communications campaigns Project Management: Develop and manage an annual integrated communications strategy that tracks Engagement and wider College communications to ensure a steady cadence of information, calls for engagement, solicitation, and stewardship Use project management software to keep the Engagement team updated and timely on all constituent communications Direct the creation, curation, and distribution of content, partnering with Marketing and Communications as well as vendors and consultants as needed Data and Analytics: Track and analyze the performance of alumni and family communications to understand what’s working and where to improve Translate data into action — refine segmentation, channel mix, timing, and messaging based on results, and test new approaches to strengthen engagement and giving Bring data-informed recommendations to the Engagement team’s strategic planning, shaping communications priorities and investments for future cycles Other Responsibilities: Completes other responsibilities as assigned. Participates as an active member of the team. Participates in department and college activities and supports implementation of shared goals and initiatives.  Provides backup support to other members of the team.   Qualifications:   Minimum 3-5 years of fundraising, development, annual giving, or nonprofit communications experience with a demonstrated record of writing effective solicitations for segmented audiences . Compensation : $68,330.00-$71,436.00 Annually Union: MAPE Benefits At Macalester, we are proud to offer excellent comprehensive employee benefits. Here are some highlights: 10% employer contributions to the retirement plan. Outstanding vacation and sick time packages, plus an additional 10 holidays. Competitive health, dental, vision, and life & disability insurance Generous employer contribution to Health Savings Account. Tuition assistance which pays between 75% - 90% of eligible tuition for employee dependents at select institutions. Free primary care for most services through Nice Healthcare when enrolled in a Macalester health plan. Access to the athletics fitness facility, wellness coaching, and activities. These are just some of the great benefits Macalester has to offer! To see our full benefits packages and options, please visit our Benefits Page Bargaining units may have slightly different benefits negotiated in their contracts. Please see applicable contracts for more details.   Satisfactory completion of a criminal background check is a condition of employment. Application Guidelines For best consideration, please submit your cover letter and resume through the Macalester Employment Opportunities webpage by August 18th. No applications will be received after this date.   Kim Price Interim - Talent Acquisition Manager price@macalester.edu Macalester College does not discriminate on the grounds of sex, gender identity, race, color, national origin, age, religion, creed, disability, marital status, familial status, pregnancy, genetic information, membership or activity in a local human rights commission, veteran status, sexual orientation, status with regard to public assistance, or other categories protected by law. For additional information, see Macalester College's full Notice of Nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://macalester.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Custodian--All-Shifts_R2026105": {
      "title": "Custodian, All Shifts",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOverview Responsibilities Requirements/Qualifications Responsibilities: Routine cleaning to include dusting, vacuuming, cleaning/washing/disinfecting surfaces, collecting and hauling trash, care of hard-surfaced and carpeted floors, cleaning restrooms and shower rooms, cleaning elevator interiors and pits Additional periodic duties may include washing exterior windows, stripping and refinishing of floors, replacing light bulbs, removing snow by shoveling and/or the use of power snow blowers, and performing necessary College event set-ups and other work as required and instructed Complete and maintain supply order requests, and insure an adequate supply stock is maintained in the building Observe building conditions and take necessary actions to maintain or repair situations by submitting work orders for repairs and performing minor repairs and reporting any loss, damage, breakage or unsafe conditions, or maintenance problems immediately Maintain security of assigned keys, building lock-up and unlocking, room opening and closing per instructions Train, work with, and/or coordinate the responsibilities of Facilities Services student employees Required  High school diploma or GED required Minimum of 1 year professional custodial or janitorial experience highly preferred. Ability to fluently read, write, and speak the English language required Ability to use all types of automatic and power cleaning equipment in association with the professional experience Ability to walk or stand for long periods of time Ability to write short work orders describing maintenance problems Physical demands required include:  Ability to perform bending, twisting, squatting, crawling, and climbing Lifting 50 lb mop bucket (on floor) so that the lip of the bucket reaches 30” height as in dumping in a sink. Lifting 50 lb box from floor level to waist level. Lifting 50 lb trash container to shoulder height as in dumping into dumpster. Must possess a valid Minnesota Driver’s License Compensation : Union: Local 70 - Maintenance Benefits At Macalester, we are proud to offer excellent comprehensive employee benefits. Here are some highlights: 10% employer contributions to the retirement plan. Outstanding vacation and sick time packages, plus an additional 10 holidays. Competitive medical, dental, vision, and life & disability insurance Generous employer contribution to Health Savings Account. Tuition assistance which pays between 75% - 100% of eligible tuition for employee dependents at select institutions. Free primary care for most services through Nice Healthcare when enrolled in a Macalester health plan. Access to the athletics fitness facility, wellness coaching, and activities. These are just some of the great benefits Macalester has to offer! To see our full benefits packages and options, please visit our Benefits Page Bargaining units may have slightly different benefits negotiated in their contracts.   Satisfactory completion of a criminal background check is a condition of employment. Application Guidelines To be considered, please submit your application. The position will remain posted until filled. Jaclyn Howard  jhoward3@macalester.edu  Talent Acquisition Manager Satisfactory completion of a criminal background check is a condition of employment. This position will undergo a federal criminal background check in accordance with the Kari Koskinen Manager Background Check Act"
    },
    "https://macalester.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Casual-Public-Safety-Officer_R2026104": {
      "title": "Casual Public Safety Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nOverview The Public Safety Dispatcher is the first point of contact for individuals seeking emergency and non-emergency services. Dispatchers will receive initial calls for service and collaborate with responders using two-way radios, telephone, email, online portals, and text messaging to communicate with staff and emergency responders for a solution that best fits department and college policies and procedures. This person will provide customer service by triaging requests and providing the best solution. The Public Safety Dispatcher will document incoming requests, activities performed, and dispositions of calls, be responsible for student workers (scheduling, hiring, training, etc.), assume responsibility for several department programs and services provided to the community (parking passes, bike registration, lost and found, etc.). Other duties may be assigned if deemed necessary by supervisors. This is a part-time position working 16 hours a week with a Friday and Saturday 6pm to 2am schedule. Additional hours on occasion. About The Department: The Department of Public Safety provides security services and emergency response on campus and develops and maintains the campus Emergency Operations Plan, a broad plan that establishes response protocol and a chain of command for emergencies that threaten the health and safety of the campus community or that disrupt its programs and activities. The plan covers emergencies ranging from natural disasters to terrorist attacks and conforms to state and federal regulations. The plan is reviewed and updated as situations, threats, and resources change. Responsibilities Qualifications Responsibilities:  Monitors campus security cameras for irregular or unusual activities. Dispatch, communicate and assist officers throughout the call. Receives incoming requests for services. Determines and implements best course of action. Records pertinent information and activities. Assists community members with lost property, parking passes and general information. Trains, schedules and monitors student dispatchers Performs other administrative duties as assigned by management Engages in and promotes Macalester’s culture of diversity and inclusion, encompassing individuals of any heritage, identity, status or orientation. Qualifications:  Radio-telephone operations and procedures, understanding of policies and procedures of receiving and processing emergency calls, call screening techniques, phone etiquette, and communicating effectively in oral and written forms.  Ability to problem solve, take decisive action, act under pressure, and effectively work with a variety of individuals from various socio- economic, ethnic and cultural backgrounds, in person and over the telephone. Must be able to understand detailed procedures that incorporate multiple campus divisions and departments. Ability to learn and to operate specialized computer systems/software, telephone, radio, and closed-circuit camera system. Compensation : Benefits At Macalester, we are proud to offer excellent comprehensive employee benefits. Here are some highlights: 10% employer contributions to the retirement plan. Outstanding vacation and sick time packages, plus an additional 10 holidays. Competitive medical, dental, vision, and life & disability insurance Generous employer contribution to Health Savings Account. Tuition assistance which pays between 75% - 100% of eligible tuition for employee dependents at select institutions. Free primary care for most services through Nice Healthcare when enrolled in a Macalester health plan. Access to the athletics fitness facility, wellness coaching, and activities. These are just some of the great benefits Macalester has to offer! To see our full benefits packages and options, please visit our Benefits Page   Satisfactory completion of a criminal background check is a condition of employment. Application Guidelines For best consideration, please submit your cover letter and resume through the Macalester Employment Opportunities webpage. This role will be posted until filled.  Satisfactory completion of a criminal background check is a condition of employment."
    }
  },
